{
  "schema": "org.disked.ntfs-capture-prototype/1",
  "status": "private-prototype-execution-contract",
  "work_id": "DE-W079",
  "scope": "Coherent bounded NTFS bootstrap observations through the existing supplied RegionReader: primary boot, primary/mirror FILE0, attributes/mappings, and mapped FILE3 volume information. Original full NTFS/provider/platform capabilities remain required.",
  "inputs": "Copy the request and reader before invoking the reader. Validate nonempty UTF8/NUL-free source ID up to128 bytes, positive epoch/source size, a contained volume window of at least512 bytes, explicit parser version3.0 or3.1, nonempty reader and all finite limits before any callback. Caller-supplied identity/epoch/version are context, not source authority or discovered format facts.",
  "reading": "Read512 boot bytes, then the full selected logical sector when needed. Use the existing boot decoder against the outer volume length. Only bootstrap_usable geometry permits the two independent physical FILE0 candidates. Every callback receives a checked absolute half-open extent inside the selected volume/source. Copy exact returned bytes before another callback. Short, oversized, null or throwing readers are typed partial-observation failures. Count every attempted callback, including final rereads, against request/byte limits. No native opening, fallback source or device enumeration.",
  "records": "Validate original FILE envelopes and all USA tails before restoring into separate bounded RAM. Keep raw hashes, header issues and partial attribute/run observations. Selected base records require flags exactly1; unknown header flags remain unsupported. When a validated USA offset is at least48, bind the optional header record number at44 to logical record0 or3; the valid older42-byte header has no such field. Attributes retain original name UTF16LE bytes and payload/mapping hashes and lengths; this collector does not render untrusted text or interpret arbitrary payloads. Decode ordinary mapping envelopes with existing checked cursors, distinguishing sparse and physical cluster zero. Enforce global attribute/run/output budgets, not only per-record limits.",
  "mirror": "Observe mirror FILE0 independently and retain both records. Compare used logical bytes after fixups while excluding only each validated USA array; unused allocation slack and USA sequence differences are not meaningful payload conflicts. Require equal used length/header layout for this selected comparison. A mismatch or invalid copy makes this bounded bootstrap inapplicable. Never substitute the mirror for primary, repair bytes or select a winning copy. This is a comparison of FILE0 only, not qualification of the complete MFT mirror.",
  "mft": "Require a complete, structurally valid in-use/non-directory base primary FILE0 and one unnamed, uncompressed, nonsparse first DATA attribute with valid complete mapping pairs and nonzero initialized data. Refuse ambiguous/duplicate DATA and ATTRIBUTE_LIST/continuation joins in this slice; retain their observations as unsupported pending original NTFS work. Require allocated bytes to equal selected mapping cluster coverage, initialized<=data<=allocated, data/initialized sizes aligned to the record size, no physical self-overlap, no intersection with boot or mirror FILE0, and logical FILE0 mappings exactly equal the initial physical candidate. Do not derive later record offsets by contiguous arithmetic.",
  "volume_record": "Read logical FILE3 only through the validated MFT mappings, splitting at run boundaries, and only wholly inside data and initialized bytes. Validate its FILE/attribute envelope and base/in-use/non-directory identity. Require exactly one unnamed resident VOLUME_INFORMATION attribute, flags0 and at least12 value bytes; reject ambiguous candidates and unjoined ATTRIBUTE_LIST. Preserve original value hash/length, observed major/minor at8/9 and raw flags at10. Observed version must equal the requested supported profile. Dirty/other flags remain observations, not filesystem health, cleanliness or recovery proofs.",
  "coherence": "Retain exact copied regions and detect unequal overlaps during collection. Once reads/parsing succeed, reread every saved region under the same budgets and compare exact bytes. Any mismatch, reader failure or insufficient reread budget withdraws applicability while preserving the observed prefix and an explicit diagnostic. Equal rereads establish only this finite region observation; no atomic snapshot, current-source permission, allocation ownership or future freshness is claimed.",
  "result": "Return owned JSON with fixed scope flags, context, boot, primary/mirror/volume record facts, MFT mapping summary, volume information, region hashes/extents, actual attempted read counters, complete/applicable and diagnostic. Invalid API inputs throw before reading; ordinary source/format/budget failures return incomplete typed results. A completed but mismatched mirror/version remains inapplicable. No callback, borrowed pointer or native resource escapes.",
  "limits": {"read_requests":512,"read_bytes":2097152,"retained_bytes":524288,"attributes":4096,"runs":4096,"output_bytes":1048576,"minimum_output_bytes":16384,"record_scratch_bytes":294912},
  "budget_accounting": "Retained-byte budget counts saved raw region bytes. Bounded record/assembly/comparison scratch is separate, at most six maximum FILE records. Output reserves8192 bytes for fixed metadata and charges every variable item before retention. Limits do not constitute an OS-enforced heap quota; contained-worker enforcement remains later work.",
  "acceptance": [
    "Independent generated sparse sources and expected physical extents/hashes; contiguous and fragmented MFT mappings including FILE3 across runs, both parser versions, sector/record/offset boundaries and exact u64 coordinates.",
    "Malformed boot/FILE/attributes/runs; ambiguous, sparse/compressed/continuation/attribute-list MFT; physical aliases; initialized/data/allocation inconsistencies; volume-information ambiguity and version mismatch. No fabricated completion or fallback read.",
    "Independent mirror payload/USA/slack distinctions; mutations in each observed region during final reread and boot-prefix overlaps; short/null/oversized/throwing callbacks; every resource budget; exact failure prefixes and absolute read bounds.",
    "Real readonly/guard callback buffers, request/callback mutation after first callback, original source immutability and fully owned deterministic returned values. Existing NTFS primitives and related reader regressions retain exact results.",
    "Exact source/compiler/header/import/build-dependency/context/manifest/tooling evidence. Selected tests are not a new complete native campaign, physical/provider admission or original0.1.0 completion. Retain W075 integration failures."
  ],
